@@ -71,6 +71,12 @@ The scripts match these prefixes exactly. Values never contain spaces;
 | `dynamite_client=returned; request_started=<0\|1>` | The existing native result line. |
 | `client_join=reset; reason=<...>` | The client session was released and re-armed (attempts may repeat). |
 | `client_join=refused; reason=<...>` | For example `placeholder_host_id` or `not_ready`. |
+| `character_config=<name\|default>; fallback=<name>; coop_ini=<0\|1>; reset_bypass_needed=<0\|1>; applied_in=TppMain.OnAllocate` | Character settings read once at startup (co-op modes only). See `docs/characters.md`. |
+| `character=<skip\|keep\|apply>; mission=<n>; requested=<name>; applied=<name\|nil>; type=<n\|nil>; reason=<...>; bypass=<0\|1>; real=<n>; start=<new\|continue\|unknown>; always=<0\|1>` | Character decision for each allocation. `start=continue` is a checkpoint or title Continue; `always=1` means the mission's continue flag was set for this allocation. New `reason=` values include `story_sequence_snake`, `title_mode`, `bypass_unavailable` and `*_sortie_kept`. |
+| `character=allocated; mission=<n>; vars=<type>; parts=<n>; camo=<n>; temp=<0\|1>; start=<...>; late=<0\|1>[; before=<type>]` | `vars` at the end of `OnAllocate` for an apply decision. `late=1` means the end-of-allocation safety net applied the type. |
+| `character=<face\|ocelot_reset_skipped\|error>; ...` | DD face set, Lua Ocelot/Quiet revert skipped once, or a contained Lua error. |
+| `character_readback=<start\|change\|manual>; verdict=<applied\|native_pending\|vars_applied\|not_applied\|keep>; expect=<type\|na>; local=<n>; vars=<type>; parts=<n>; camo=<n>; temp=<0\|1>; players=<ready\|stopped\|native_unavailable\|stage>; limit=<n\|na>; i0=<n\|na\|err>; i1=<n\|na\|err>; raw0=<n\|na>; raw1=<n\|na>; quiet_ocelot_read_as=0` | Lab-only character readback (needs `lab.ini` and an apply/keep decision). `verdict=applied` means `vars.playerType` and the local native slot both equal `expect`. |
+| `player_type_patch=<active\|inactive\|refused\|failed>; ...` | Native Ocelot/Quiet reset bypass state. |
 
